"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204003912\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Transient Witch\"><img alt=\"Transient Witch\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"25\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Expert Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/25?cb=20110204003912\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/f5/D012_Phoenix_Down.png/revision/latest?cb=20120409211126\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Phoenix Down\"><img alt=\"Phoenix Down\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"10\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Phoenix Down.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Phoenix_Down.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/f5/D012_Phoenix_Down.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/10?cb=20120409211126\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Multichain at C4 to get all enemies here.\n</p><p>The line-up is the Party piece, consisting of a Level 89 Counterfeit Wraith with Atomos and a Level 121 Imaginary Brawler. Then comes a Level 91 Transient Witch with Deathgaze, and a Level 90 Imaginary Champion with Bahamut and Imaginary Soldier. I miss being able to go more in-depth on the enemies kiddies, but now they all have the same movesets and accessories, mostly, even between different types, so what can I do?\n</p><p>The chest has a Titan's Tear, a unique trade accessory. It unlocks the Giant's equipment - Giant's Axe, Giant's Gloves, Giant's Helm, and Giant's Harness. This set <i>isn't</i> entirely useless and in fact is quite use<i>ful</i>. When three pieces are worn together they trigger the Pride of the Titans combination, giving you an extra 100 base Bravery and 750 more HP. Though the pieces are only level 90, this boost is more than what you'd get if you traded out the Helm and Harness for Level 100 gear. Thus the only penalty you get for opting for Giant's gear over Level 100 stuff is slightly lower defenses. And as a three-piece combination, you only need the three armor pieces and can still use a Level 100 weapon for no power loss.\n</p><p>Grab the Phoenix Down if anyone has died and head down.\n<br style=\"clear:both\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-d