:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>We have no chain skills worth using here, we'll save our two Jump Chains for later in the gateway.\n</p><p>Fight the Ultimate enemy first, it's a Level 127 Transient Witch with Omega. I say fight her first to get to the chest, which has a random chain skill, if you're fortunate enough to get a skill that let's you chain some of the enemies, yay. Otherwise fight the Party piece, then beat your Assist and manually chain the last two enemies. The Party is a Level 90 Imaginary Champion with Bahamut and an Imaginary Soldier, and a Level 100 Transient Lion with the Magus Sisters and a Transient Gunner. The two Experts, of course, a Level 90 Fallacious Tree with Asura and a Level 90 Phantasmal Harlequin with Tiamat. Because, ya know, we've fought these enemy types a dozen times already and kicked their asses thanks to our level advantage, but surely this time, they will be victorious!\n<br style=\"clear:both\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description im