r=\"cabd62\"><b>AC</b>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Now is the time for a Jump Chain - use one at C4 to get four enemies, since the purple emblem is a KP +1 booster, yay!\n</p><p>First is a Level 129 Warrior of Antiquity with Omega, and an unknown Assist but really it's probably an Idle Sky Pirate. Zidane made awesome use of the Iron Giant summon here, it worked much more efficiently than Carbuncle and with the winds of the arena he was able to quickly Break the Warrior while whittling down his HP, at which point I let him hit me a couple times to recover his Bravery, then whittled him back down and Broke him again to end the match. Then, a Level 128 Ephemeral Phantom with Omega, once again Iron Giant was helpful, I used Free Energy to get him down to the point the Break would let me kill him, thus avoiding that pesky Omega throwing off my groove. Then comes the considerably easier Level 91 Transient Witch with Kraken and a Level 91 Capricious Reaper with Calcabrina or a Capricious Thief.\n</p><p>With 32 KP in our pocket, there's one enemy left of course, a Level 128 Lady of Antiquity with Ultima Weapon. The Initial BRV boost helps, true she begins with 9999 Bravery, but the stage will quickly sap that into the Bravery pool to become ours once Carbuncle goes off.\n</p><p>The chest, what a shock, random skill!\n<br style=\"clear:both\" />\n</p